2 CONT [...Paykar Khān Igīrmī Dūrt  rose to influence in 1608, when Shah Abbas I appointed him governor of Barda. Around 1620, he was, further, given the governorship of Kakheti, a neighboring Georgian kingdom, which the shah sought to b
2 CONC ring under his full control. On this occasion, Abbas gave to Paykar in marriage Lela (Fatma Sultan Begum),[2] a royal princess from another Georgian kingdom, that of Kartli, whom the shah dismissed from his harem after having her 
2 CONC brother, King Luarsab II of Kartli, executed. ] ref https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paykar_Khan_Igirmi_Durt
