1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Paata Abelovich Andronikashvili was a prominent Georgian nobleman from the influential House of Andronikashvili (later known as the Princes Andronikov in the Russian Empire).
2 CONT
2 CONT * Lineage: He was the son of Abel Garsevanovich Andronikashvili and Princess Ketevan, who was the daughter of King Heraclius I (Erekle I) of Kakheti.
2 CONT * The Chronology Fix: Because his mother Ketevan died in 1718 and his father was active into the early 18th century, Paata was likely born right around or shortly after 1693. However, he lived well into the mid-1700s.
2 CONT
2 CONT The most definitive proof that the 1712 death date is wrong lies in his children. Paata Abelovich had several sons who went on to become major figures in Georgian history during the late 18th century:
2 CONT
2 CONT * David (Datuna) Paatovich Andronikashvili: A high-ranking official and diplomat.
2 CONT * Melkisedek (Malkhaz) Paatovich Andronikashvili: Born much later in the 18th century, he was a key figure whose own son, Ivan Malkhazovich Andronikov (1798–1868), became a famous General of the Cavalry in the Russian Imperial Arm
2 CONC y.
2 CONT * Tamaz (Toma/Foma) Paatovich Andronikashvili: whose lineage is thoroughly tracked through Georgian nobility registries.
