2 CONT Count Pavel Dmitrievich Kiselyov or Kiseleff (Па́вел Дми́триевич Киселёв) (January 19 [O.S. January 8] 1788, Moscow — November 26 [O.S. November 14] 1872, Paris) is generally regarded as the most brilliant Russian reformer during 
2 CONC Nicholas I's generally reactionary reign.
