1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Prince Sergei Nikitich Troubetzkoy (1829-1899) - Russian military and courtier from the Troubetzkoy family, chief marshal, actual privy councilor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography The youngest son of Prince Nikita Petrovich Troubetzkoy and his wife Alexandra Alexandrovna Nelidova. The nephew of the failed dictator of the Decembrists. Godson of the chamber-maid of honor EI Nelidova [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Educated in the Corps of Pages and released from it with the rights of the 1st category in 1849 [2]; On May 26, 1849, he was promoted from page-chamber to ensign of the Preobrazhensky Life Guards Regiment. He devoted the first hal
2 CONC f of his life to military service: in 1855 he was appointed adjutant to His Imperial Highness, Grand Duke Mikhail Nikolaevich; promoted to colonel in 1862; On November 8, 1866 he was promoted to major general, with the abandonment
2 CONC  of the governor of the Caucasus; in 1871 he was appointed to the Retinue of His Imperial Majesty. In 1873-1878 he was the head of the field office of the governor of the Caucasus. Was awarded the orders: St. Stanislaus 1st Art. (
2 CONC 1870), St. Anne 1st Art. (1874), St. Vladimir 2nd Art. (1878), White eagle with swords (1878) [3].
2 CONT
2 CONT He participated in the Russian-Turkish war (1877-1878) and was promoted to lieutenant general on November 8, 1877 for his distinction against the Turks. After retiring from military service, he transferred to the service of the co
2 CONC urt and in 1884, by the Imperial order, was appointed as a knight marshal of the Imperial court, with renaming into privy councilors, from August 30, 1888 - the chief marshal of the Imperial court, a real privy councilor. He was a
2 CONC warded the Order of St. Alexander Nevsky (1887) with diamond signs (1893) [3].
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1888, the Hermitage was entrusted with his management, but due to departures from St. Petersburg for a long time, he was never approved by the director of the museum. In the halls of the museum at that time, court balls and din
2 CONC ners were especially often held, and Academician A. A. Kunik, curator of the Russian part of the numismatics collection, was engaged in the affairs of the Hermitage. In 1889, I.A.Vsevolozhsky was appointed director of the Hermitag
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sofya Trubetskaya with children According to AA Polovtsev, Troubetzkoy "was a sweet man, completely devoted to the details of his petty court and high society life" [4].
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to the highest Russian orders, he had numerous awards from foreign states: the Bavarian Order of St. Michael, 3rd Art. (1852), order of the Netherlands lion, 3rd class. (1852), Neapolitan Order of St. Francis (1852), C
2 CONC onstantine Order of St. George (1852), Hesse-Darmstadt Order of Philip the Magnanimous 4th Art. (1852), Württemberg Order of the Crown (1852), French Order of the Legion of Honor Officer Cross (1852), Sardinian Order of St. Maurit
2 CONC ius and Lazarus, 2nd class. (1857), Persian Order of the Lion and the Sun 1st century. (1869), Baden order of the Zeringen lion, 2nd class. with a star (1870), Turkish Medjidie Order, 2nd class. with a star (1872), Persian portrai
2 CONC t of the Shah with diamonds (1881), Austrian Order of the Iron Crown 1st Art. (1884), Prussian Order of the Crown 1st Art. (1884), Austrian Order of Leopold 1st Art. (1886), Montenegrin order of Prince Daniel I 1st century (1886),
2 CONC  Mecklenburg-Schwerin Order of the Vendian Crown Grand Cross 1st Art. (1886), Prussian Order of the Red Eagle 1st Art. (1889) [3].
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in June 1899 from pneumonia in Stuttgart and was buried next to his mother at the Novodevichy cemetery in St. Petersburg [5].
2 CONT
2 CONT A family Wife (from April 20, 1876) [6] - Princess Sofia Iraklievna Bagration-Mukhranskaya (1850-1932), granddaughter of the last appanage ruler Mukhransky (1800-1801) and sister of Prince Alexander Bagration-Mukhransky. For her h
2 CONC usband's merits, she was awarded a lady of the Order of St. Catherine (small cross) (07.22.1891). They had sons in marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Nikita Sergeevich (1877-1963), colonel, adjutant of Grand Duke Nikolai Mikhailovich; in exile, the chairman of the Union of Pages and the Society of Zealots of Russian Military Antiquity; since 1917 he has been married to the ball
2 CONC erina Lyubov Egorova. Pyotr Sergeevich (1882-1958), graduate of the Corps of Pages, officer of the 17th Dragoon Regiment; emigrated to England. Notes
2 CONT  TsGIA SPb. F. 362. - Op. 2. - D. 1. - P. 116. Metric books of the Church of the Tauride Palace.
2 CONT  Pages for 183 years (1711-1894): Biographies of former pages with portraits / comp. Freiman O.R .. - Friedrichshamn, 1894 .-- P. 447.
2 CONT  Prince Troubetzkoy Sergei Nikitich // List of civilian ranks of the first III classes: Rev. until 1st Oct. 1894 - P. 85.
2 CONT  Polovtsov A. A. Diary of the Secretary of State. In 2 volumes. - M .: Tsentrpoligraf, 2005 .-- T. 1. - P. 296.
2 CONT  Petersburg necropolis / Comp. V.I.Saitov. - SPb .: Printing house of M.M. Stasyulevich, 1912 .-- T. 4. - P. 297.
2 CONT  TsGIA SPb. f.19. op. 124. d. 1264. p. 153. Metric books of the Church of His Majesty's Vicar in the Caucasus. 
