1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Prince '''Nikita Sergeievitch Trubetzkoy'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 07/01/1877, Tiflis - 08/31/1963, Petit-Clamaret, Paris, France Orthodox. Father - actual privy councilor Sergei Nikitich, mother - Sophia Iraklievna ur. Princess Bagration-Mukhranskaya.
2 CONT
2 CONT Education: Corps of Pages (1898, 1st category, in the 44th Dragoon Nizhny Novgorod Regiment). Ranks: entered the service (1.09.1896), cornet with st. 08.13.1897 (High pr. 1898), lieutenant (Art. 08.13.1901), staff captain (Art. 08
2 CONC .13.1905), captain (Art. 08.13.1909), transferred to the Guard (1913 or 1914), colonel ... Service: he studied in the Corps of Pages (1893-1898, entered the 5th grade), in the 44th Dragoon Nizhny Novgorod regiment, adjutant led. P
2 CONC rince Nikolai Mikhailovich (before 09/01/1912 - after 09/01/1913). Awards: A3 (High pr. 1909), C2 (High pr. 1912).
2 CONT
2 CONT Other information: in exile in France, in 1934 treasurer, secretary and member of the court of honor of the main board of the Union of Pages, by Feb. 1954 Chairman of the Union of Pages, 1934 General Secretary of the Society of Fr
2 CONC iends of the "Sentinel", 1939 supported the leader. Prince Vladimir Kirillovich; board member of the Union of Officers of the Caucasian Army in Paris, secretary of the regimental association of the 17th dragoon regiment, chairman 
2 CONC of the Society of Zealots of Russian Military Antiquity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Works:
2 CONT
2 CONT Nizhny Novgorod saber // Mollo "Russian edged weapons". Paris, 196? Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Volkov S.V. Army Cavalry Officers: The Martyrology Experience. - M .: Russian way, 2004. List of captains of army cavalry by seniority, 1.09.1912.
2 CONT
2 CONT List of captains of army cavalry by seniority, 09/01/1913.
2 CONT
2 CONT von Freiman O.R. Pages for 185 Years, no. 9, Friedrichshamn, 1897. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince '''Nikita Sergeievitch Trubetzkoy''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dates of life: 1.07.1877, Tiflis - 31.08.1963, Petit-Clamaret, Paris, France Biography: Orthodox. Father - actual privy councilor Sergei Nikitich, mother - Sophia Iraklievna ur. Princess Bagration-Mukhranskaya. Education: Corps of
2 CONC  Pages (1898, 1st category, in the 44th Dragoon Nizhny Novgorod Regiment). Transferred to the Guard (1913 or 1914) Studied at the Corps of Pages (1893-1898, entered the 5th grade), in the 44th Dragoon Nizhny Novgorod Regiment, adj
2 CONC utant led. Prince Nikolai Mikhailovich (before 09/01/1912 - after 09/01/1913). In exile in France, in 1934 treasurer, secretary and member of the court of honor of the main board of the Union of Pages, by Feb. 1954 Chairman of the
2 CONC  Union of Pages, 1934 General Secretary of the Society of Friends of the "Sentinel", 1939 supported the leader. Prince Vladimir Kirillovich; board member of the Union of Officers of the Caucasian Army in Paris, secretary of the re
2 CONC gimental association of the 17th dragoon regiment, chairman of the Society of Zealots of Russian Military Antiquity. Compositions: Nizhny Novgorod saber // Mollo "Russian edged weapons". Paris, 196?
2 CONT
2 CONT Ranks: Entered the service on 1.09.1896 Cornet with st. 08/13/1897 (VP 1898) Lieutenant (Art.13.08.1901) staff captain (art.13.08.1905) on January 1, 1909. - 17th Dragoon Nizhny Novgorod His Majesty Regiment, Staff Captain Captain
2 CONC  (art.13.08.1909) Colonel of the Guard 
2 CONT
2 CONT Awards: A3 (High pr. 1909), C2 (High pr. 1912).
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional Information: -Search for the full name of the "Card index of the Bureau for the registration of losses on the fronts of the First World War 1914-1918." in RGVIA -Links to this person from other pages of the site "RIA Of
2 CONC ficers" Sources: Volkov S.V. Army Cavalry Officers: The Martyrology Experience. - M .: Russian way, 2004. List of captains of army cavalry by seniority, 1.09.1912. List of captains of army cavalry by seniority, 09/01/1913. von Fre
2 CONC iman O.R. Pages for 185 Years, no. 9, Friedrichshamn, 1897. 
