1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nekliudov, Anatoli Vasilievich (4.IV.1856+25.IX.1943).  Educated  at the Imperial Nikolaevski Lyceum in Moscow,  graduate in Law from the University (1879),  Secretary of the Russian Legation in Constantinople (188
2 CONC 3-1891),  Secretary of the Russian Legation in Belgrade (1891~1898),  Secretary of the Russian Legation at Stuttgart (1898~1904),  Chamberlain (1903),  Councillor of the Russian Ambassy in Paris (1904~1911),  Russian Ambassador in
2 CONC  Sofia (1911~1913),  Russian Ambassador in Stockholm (1913~1917),  Privy Coucillor (1916),  Ambassador of the Provisional Government in Madrid (1917),  retired (1917).  Died in Nice.  His memoirs were published in English in 1920 
2 CONC and he wrote and published an interesting work on his family (in  Russian).
