2 CONT Irakli Gruzinsky (Georgian: ირაკლი გრუზინსკი; Russian: Ираклий Александрович Грузинский, Irakly Aleksandrovich Gruzinsky; August 18, 1826 – April 27, 1882) was a Georgian prince of the House of Bagrationi and a colonel in the Russ
2 CONC ian Imperial army. He was a grandson of Heraclius II, the penultimate king of Georgia, and the son of Prince Alexander, a staunch opponent of the Russian possession of Georgia.
