1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *[http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FsTVF0Fu5_c&feature=related Prince Igor - Polovtsian Dances ],  
2 CONT *[http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QfeAtryEEZ4&feature=related String Quartet No 2 D major 1st and intro of 2nd Mov],  
2 CONT *[http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z3e6CPLBZWI Symphony No. 2. 1st Mvt.],  
2 CONT *[http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rQY51GFECbo Borodin Nocturne].  
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Borodin  '''Alexander Porfiryevich Borodin'''] (12 November 1833 – 27 February 1887) was a Russian Romantic composer and chemist of Georgian–Russian parentage. He was a member of the group o
2 CONC f composers called The Five (or "The Mighty Handful"), who were dedicated to producing a specifically Russian kind of art music. He is best known for his symphonies, his two string quartets, and his opera Prince Igor. Music from P
2 CONC rince Igor and his string quartets was later adapted for the US musical Kismet.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://all-art.org/music/borodin.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://cdn2.all-art.org/music/music_files/borodin_Polovtsian%20Dances.mp3 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://all-art.org/history661_music.html 
2 CONT
