1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I would be grateful to people that they NOT change the profile of my aunt and Godmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT To the best of my knowledge, Princess Liubov Alexandrovna Obolenskaya (see http://www.geni.com/people/Princess-Liubov-Alexandrovna-Obolenskaya/6000000020623432820) née Narishkina, and her husband Prince Serguei (Sergei) Alexandrov
2 CONC ich Obolensky (see http://www.geni.com/people/Prince-Serguei-Alexandrovich-Obolensky/6000000020623503724) had six children. Their children were Prince Alexander Sergueievich Obolensky; Maria Sergeievna Ranicar née Princess Obolens
2 CONC kaya; Prince Feodor Sergueievich Obolensky; Prince Mikhail Sergeievich Obolensky; Princess Lubov Sergeievna who married Clive Wilfrid Salter in Nairobi, and Princess Irina Sergeievna Obolenskaya (married first to Sir Edward Beddin
2 CONC gton Behrens in London on August 9, 1944 and divorced in 1958 - then she married George Morton on May 12, 1958).
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Liubov Alexandrovna Obolenskaya was not an only child, she was the half-sister of my father Vadim Alexandrovich Narishkin (see http://www.geni.com/people/Vadim-Alexandrovich-Narishkin/6000000010533418462)
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted by Vera Vadimovna Narishkina (http://www.geni.com/people/Vera-Vadimovna-Narishkina/6000000010532989954)
2 CONT
