1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Alexandra Nikolaevna Ignatieva (Osten-Sacken)''', Countess (von der) (December 29, 1909, Tsarskoye Selo, Petersburg Province - November 29, 1989, New Kakhovka, Ukraine). Teacher.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter N.V. and S.N. Osten-Sakenov, sister of Ekaterina N. and Vladimir N. Osten-Sakenov.
2 CONT
2 CONT In exile in France since 1922, she received secondary education. From 1941 she lived in Tangier (Morocco). She worked as a secretary, took an active part in the life of the Russian colony, helped refugees with translations and pap
2 CONC erwork. In 1957 she left for the USSR (to her husband and daughter). Worked as a teacher of foreign languages.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT * [http://www.dommuseum.ru/old/index.php?m=dist&pid=7675 Biographical Dictionary RUSSIAN ABROAD IN FRANCE]
