1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Prince "Mykolas Trubeckis" (Michail Grigorjevič Trubeckoj)
2 CONT   No later than 1940 July 4 Photo from the personal document
2 CONT   Topic: 03. Lithuania during the USSR occupation (1940-1990), 32. National minorities
2 CONT
2 CONT The photo is pasted in the foreign passport of Lithuania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince M. Trubeckis (Michail Grigorjevič Trubeckoj) was born in 1905, in Constantinople, Turkey, in the family of the secretary of the Russian mission in Turkey. After the October coup in Russia, he left Moscow with his mother and
2 CONC  brothers to go abroad. In France, he obtained the specialty of engineer-radioelectrician. Not wanting to serve in the French army and based on his "Lithuanian origin", in 1938 arrived in Kaunas, received Lithuanian citizenship. H
2 CONC e stayed in Lithuania because "he was the only specialist in radio receivers", he worked as a radio engineer at the Press Fund. At the invitation of the wife of the Minister of Foreign Affairs, Marija Urbšienė, he attended parties
2 CONC  at her house, where he met diplomats from foreign countries and many "Lithuanian elites". Soviet security in 1941 April 18 arrested "as a representative of the monarchist circle", "associated with bourgeois governments", on suspi
2 CONC cion of espionage against the USSR. After the beginning of the USSR-German war, in 1941 in June was released from Kaunas hard labor prison. During the Second World War, he went to Paris. After the war, his search was announced. in
2 CONC  1964 the criminal case was terminated in the absence of "criminal data".
2 CONT
2 CONT Died in 1989 Canada, Montreal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Mykolas Trubeckis in the internal prison of the People's Commissariat of State Security of the Lithuanian SSR (NKGB) in Kaunas 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://lyavaizdai.archyvai.lt/vaizdai/3/doc8169 
