1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born Rostock, Germany. In the 1960-s he managed Russian and Eastern European BBC broadcasting. He graduated from the Lycee Francais Brussels, Lille and Trinity College, Dublin. Took part in the WWII. Captain in the
2 CONC  British Army. Expert on Russian affairs at the Foreign office. He was married first (London 18 Sep 1946) to Veronica Monahan (Muzzaffarpur, India 18 Oct 1917-London 18 Dec 1979); secondly (July 1981) to Joanna Edgecumbe-Rendle (b
2 CONC orn 18 July 1921).<br/>
