1 NAME Hugo Joseph Elzear Anton von Padua Marie Gangolf /Kálnoky de Kőröspatak/ GR
2 GIVN Hugo Joseph Elzear Anton von Padua Marie Gangolf
2 NSFX GR
2 _MARNM Kálnoky de Kőröspatak
1 NAME Hugo Graf Kálnoky de Köröspatak
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 MAY 1900
2 PLAC Hietzing
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vienna
3 STAE Vienna
3 CTRY Austria
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 JUN 1955
2 ADDR
3 CITY Washington D.C.
3 STAE DC
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gróf újságíró
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00063857&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Hugo, Graf Kálnoky von Köröspatak, was born 11 May 1900 at Hietzing near Vienna in Austria, the son of Hugo, Graf Kálnoky von Köröspatak, and Maria, Gräfin zu Herberstein. Sepsiköröspatak, the family's ancestral seat nea
2 CONC r Kronstadt in Transylvania, was seven hundred years old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28 June 1934 in Burg Ranis, Germany, he married Ingeborg von Breitenbuch, the daughter of Dietrich von Breitenbuch and Herta Rasmuss. They became the parents of four children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In January 1945 his pregant wife, their three children and Cuci, their nurse, left Hungary to escape the approaching Russian army. Because of a Gestapo warrant for his arrest, he could not accompany them. He had earned his place o
2 CONC n the Gestapo wanted list with a series of articles for his Budapest newspaper, the _Pesterlloyd._ Praising Churchill and criticizing German policies, some parts of these articles had been picked up for broadcast by the BBC. Frien
2 CONC ds in the underground had warned him of his impending arrest, and they were able to flee Budapest just hours before the Gestapo raided his house. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After the Second World War the family moved to the United States, where Hugo and Ingeborg divorced on 4 December 1953. Hugo died on 24 June 1955 in Washington D.C..
