1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Prince Igor Nikolayevich Troubetskoy (Troubetzkoy)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Igor Nikolayevich Troubetzkoy (Russian: Игорь Николаевич Трубецкой, 23 August 1912 - 20 December 2008) was the driver of the first Ferrari to ever compete in Grand Prix Motor Racing. He drove a 2-litre Ferrari "Tipo" 166 in
2 CONC  Monaco on May 16, 1948. Earlier that year he had won the Targa Florio with the Ferrari 166 Sport Allemano Spyder (chassis # 001S, only one built). He was married to Barbara Hutton, one of the richest women of the time, between 19
2 CONC 47 and 1951.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/160350074/igor_nikolayevich-troubetzkoy
